docs {
  # Services APIs

  This folder contains bill/service purchase endpoints for the mobile app.

  ## Data Service Flow

  The frontend should only call BillXpress endpoints. Do not call UjayData directly from the app.

  Current data provider:

  ```txt
  ujaydata
  ```

  The backend is built so admin can switch to another provider later without changing the frontend endpoints.

  ## Live Pricing Rule

  Data plans are fetched live from the active provider whenever the frontend calls:

  ```txt
  GET /api/v1/services/data/plans
  ```

  The backend then applies the BillXpress markup percentage.

  Example:

  ```txt
  Provider price: N200
  Normal user markup: 15%
  User sees: N230

  Vendor markup: 10%
  Vendor sees: N220
  ```

  The frontend should display `sellingPrice`, not `costPrice`.

  ## Data Purchase Rule

  When buying data, frontend sends:

  ```json
  {
    "planId": "136",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "transactionPin": "1234"
  }
  ```

  Backend will:

  1. Fetch the live plan again.
  2. Recalculate the current selling price.
  3. Verify transaction PIN.
  4. Debit wallet.
  5. Call the active provider.
  6. Refund wallet automatically if provider fails.
  7. Send notification/email.

  This protects the app from stale prices and failed provider requests.

  ## UjayData Purchase ID Note

  UjayData plan response contains both `pId` and `planid`.

  For purchase, BillXpress uses `pId` by default. In our API response this is:

  ```txt
  providerPlanId
  ```

  The frontend should still send only the normal `id` from our plan response. The backend handles the provider mapping.
}
